  "year": 2012,
  "pointsSystem": "Two-tier relative placement scoring. Twelve events used a 100-point table (1st=100, 2nd=95, 3rd=90, 4th=85, 5th=80, then descending by smaller steps to 30th=27); three short tests (Broad Jump #2012-04, Ball Toss #2012-05, Sprint #2012-08) used a 50-point table (1st=50, 2nd=48, 3rd=46 ... 30th=17). Ties took the higher placement; time-capped events added 1 second per missing rep; max-effort events used 0.01 partial units per secondary-movement rep as tiebreaks. Final overall placing is the sum of event points.",
